\description{
A multiscale conservative frame family divides one fixed global budget
between its scales, and it divides it by the weights the analyst chose:
the \code{total} component summed over the rows of scale \eqn{s} is exactly
\eqn{\alpha_s G_\Omega}{alpha_s * G_Omega} whatever the data say
(\code{design/conservative-geometry-contract.md} section 3.1). What the data do
decide is how each scale's fixed budget splits into a coherent and a
configuration part. \code{coherence_spectrum()} reports that split, per scale
and -- with \code{by_location = TRUE} -- per (scale, location).
}
\details{
